  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Description",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "heading"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "A user who has been given the Schedule but deliberately not given Work Orders: View can still read the whole work order list down the left of the Schedule page \u2014 customer names, unit numbers, how many lines each job has, the hours estimate and the lead technician. That is exactly the information their permissions were set up to keep from them, and the restriction can be got round simply by opening the Schedule.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Steps to reproduce",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "heading"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ],
       "text": "Environment: ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": "QA branch sv8685 \u2014 https://sv8685.qa.shopview.com/schedule. Desktop browser, with the location Staging Heavy Duty - 9919 selected. Steps 1 to 3 are done signed in as an Admin; from step 4 you are signed in as the restricted user made in step 1.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "order": 1
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "Signed in as an Admin, go to Settings then Roles & Permissions and create a role with Schedule: View switched ON and Work Orders: View switched OFF, and nothing else switched on.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "Go to Settings then Staff, open any active staff member, set their Role to that new role and save.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "Sign out.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "Sign in as that staff member.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "Open Schedule from the top navigation.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "Read the left-hand panel.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "When you are finished, delete the role you made and put the staff member back on their original role.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "orderedList"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Current behaviour",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "heading"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The full work order list is shown \u2014 18 cards, each with the work order number, the customer name, the unit number, 'N lines - Xh Est.', the technician initials and the lead technician's name. Nothing is hidden.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "For a developer: this is not only a screen problem \u2014 the request that fetches the sidebar's work orders also succeeds for this user and returns the full list. The permission tier itself is enforced correctly, though: the same user is refused when trying to create, change or delete a shift or an event.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Expected behaviour",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "heading"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The left-hand panel hides the work order list for this user. They can still see the calendar and everyone's shifts, but no customer names, unit numbers, line counts, hours or lead technicians.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "type": "rule"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Source",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "heading"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Epic SV-8685, story SV-8687 (Work Order Sidebar & Mini Calendar), and the Schedule specification (Confluence page 713031682), version 25.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Section 14.2 (Work order sidebar dependency): \"The left panel sidebar displays work order data (customer, unit, lines, lead tech) and requires Work Orders: View to populate. If a user has Schedule access but Work Orders: View is OFF, the sidebar hides the work order list and line drill-down (the mini calendar remains available). The user can still view and interact with shifts already on the grid, but cannot drag new ones from the sidebar since the WO list is not visible.\"",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
